// SuperTrend flip to bullish, taken only when the plan behind it is acceptable.
// SUPERTREND_FLIP_BULL = 1 on the bar where SuperTrend(10, 3.0) changed from
// bearish to bullish, 0 otherwise. The host computes it from the SUPERTREND_DIR
// kernel in nano/indicators/ - or its own equivalent - and publishes the change
// as a 0/1 series; Nano compares the published number and nothing else.
// STOP_DISTANCE_ATR = (entry - protective stop) / ATR(10), where the host places
// the stop below the flip bar or the swing low the flip broke. TARGET_R =
// planned target distance / planned stop distance, both in points, both
// host-computed. ATR_PCT = ATR(10) as a percentage of price.
// PARAMETERS - every number in this rule is one of these three floors, and each
// one is named so it can be argued with rather than absorbed:
//   volatility floor    ATR_PCT >= 0.05           a flip in a dead tape is noise
//   risk floor          STOP_DISTANCE_ATR >= 0.5  the stop must sit outside the
//                                                 noise it is meant to survive
//   reward:risk floor   TARGET_R >= 2.33          the target must be worth the
//                                                 risk the stop already defines
// WHAT THIS RULE REFUSES TO DO: it does not carry the stop price, the target
// price, or a quantity. Nano's intent vocabulary is buy/sell/execute/pause/
// observe plus a confidence - there is no field for a price level or a size - so
// the host that published STOP_DISTANCE_ATR and TARGET_R must recompute the
// bracket and own it. The rule asserts only that on this bar a plan clearing all
// three floors existed. It is not evidence that the plan works.
// REGIME: trend initiation after a bearish leg. Do NOT fire in a range - inside
// a range the band is broken in both directions repeatedly and the flip becomes
// a metronome. The ATR_PCT floor is the cheap version of that filter and not a
// substitute for knowing the regime.
// CONDITIONS: all four, AND-chained. Only the first is about what price did; the
// other three are the host asserting a tradeable plan exists.
// INVALIDATION: a close back under the SuperTrend line. Note the line and the
// rule's stop are different levels - the indicator trails its own band while the
// stop sits under structure - so the two can disagree, and the host decides
// which one governs.
// SHAPE: 15m; a bearish band flipping to a bullish one under price, with enough
// range in the bar for a stop to sit clear of the noise.
// NOT golden_cross: that is a slow persistent state and reads as a regime
// filter; this is a discrete event on a single bar. NOT donchian_breakout: that
// requires price through a prior extreme, this requires only the band to flip,
// which can happen well inside one. NOT atr_volatility_halt: that uses ATR_PCT
// as a ceiling to stand down, this uses the same series as a floor to stand up -
// not opposites, and both can be true of the same violent tape.
// CALIBRATED ON: MNQ futures, 15m. The three floors are scale-free ratios and
// travel across instruments; the 15m bar does not - on a slower chart the same
// flip carries a much larger stop in points for the same 0.5 ATR.
strategy SupertrendFlipLong {

    every 15m {

        if SUPERTREND_FLIP_BULL(10) >= 1 and ATR_PCT(10) >= 0.05 and STOP_DISTANCE_ATR(10) >= 0.5 and TARGET_R >= 2.33 {

            buy(MNQ, 0.7)

        }

    }

}
